Steps 1- Register The Domain Name
-Navigate over to Route 53
-Click "Registered Doamin"
-Write in whatever domain name you prefer
-Click for availability and add to cart
- Fills in contact details and accept Terms and Conditions when finished

Keep in mind, the domain name registration may take up to 3 days to fully complete. But usually it's up and running with an hour 

Step 2- Setting up S3 bucket
-Navigate to the S3 bucket
-Click create a bucket
-Use the Route 53 domain name you choosed as the bucket name
-Be sure to choose the corresponding AWS Region, as this helps with lower latency
-Uncheck "Block All Public Access"
-Finish creating bucket
-Once bucket is available, select upload and choose whatever file you wish to display
-Click on properties and enable "Static Website Hosting" at the bottom
-Be sure to fill in "index.html" and "error.html" and click save change 
-Next, navigate to the permission tab and scroll down to bucket policy
-Click edit  and saved the following bucket policy

{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "PublicReadGetObject",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": "*",
            "Action": [
                "s3:GetObject"
            ],
            "Resource": [
                "arn:aws:s3:::Bucket-Name/*"
            ]
        }
    ]
} 

Be sure to replace the "arn:aws:s3" with your own, which can be found under the uploaded file properties tabs
